  "result": "Perfect! All 103 tests pass. I've added line discounts to the invoice system:\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`lineDiscount(line)`** \u2014 Calculates discount for a single line: `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent \u00f7 100`, rounded to whole cents.\n\n2. **Updated `createInvoice`** \u2014 Now accepts `discountPercent` (0-100, can be decimal like 12.5) in line input; validates and defaults to 0 if not provided.\n\n3. **Updated `addLine`** \u2014 Accepts optional `discountPercent` in input with same validation; defaults to 0 for new lines.\n\n4. **Updated `invoiceTotals`** \u2014 Returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n   - `subtotal` = sum of line totals (before discounts)\n   - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n   - `total` = subtotal - discount (clamped at 0, never negative)\n\n**Added error code:** `DISCOUNT_INVALID` for values outside 0-100 or non-numeric.\n\n**Key design decision:** No amount computed anywhere can go below zero \u2014 all totals are clamped at 0.\n\n**Tests added (18 new):**\n- Discount acceptance and validation in createInvoice/addLine\n- Decimal discount percentages\n- Line discount calculations\n- Invoice totals with varying discounts\n- Multi-line invoices with different discounts per line\n- Total clamping at 0\n\nAll 103 tests pass. \u2705",
